      "id": "6wq06zo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi (1869–1948) played a central role in India's independence movement.",
        "Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858) was one of the earliest prominent figures fighting against British rule.",
        "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931) represented the revolutionary youth phase of the freedom struggle.",
        "The Lal-Bal-Pal trio consists of Lala Lajpat Rai (1865–1928), Bal Gangadhar Tilak (1856–1920), and Bipin Chandra Pal (1858–1932).",
        "Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (1875–1950) and Jawaharlal Nehru (1889–1964) were key post-independence leaders."
      ],
      "id": "xc2g1a4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4q7bmlh",
      "content": "• Known as the 'Father of the Nation'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "45vwi43",
      "content": "• Leader of the Indian National Movement."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q62rd4z",
      "content": "• Introduced Satyagraha and non-violent resistance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vonfdkj",
      "content": "• Led Non-Cooperation (1920), Civil Disobedience (1930), Quit India (1942)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ks166dh",
      "content": "• Led the Dandi March in 1930."
    },
    {
      "id": "ehs54bh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Subhas Chandra Bose (1897–1945)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7gkvxxt",
      "content": "• Popularly known as Netaji."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wari6sk",
      "content": "• Founded the Indian National Army (INA)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9aqvf8a",
      "content": "• Gave the slogan 'Give me blood and I will give you freedom'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "szc1r5s",
      "content": "• Formed the Azad Hind Government."
    },
    {
      "id": "t20dmvc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Bhagat Singh (1907–1931)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tg6l9hq",
      "content": "• Famous revolutionary freedom fighter."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qvsve0k",
      "content": "• Involved in the Lahore Conspiracy Case."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9ovq03p",
      "content": "• Along with Batukeshwar Dutt threw bombs in the Central Legislative Assembly in 1929."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4p5jmlz",
      "content": "• Executed by the British in 1931."
    },
    {
      "id": "jcn4vxa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Rani Lakshmibai (1828–1858)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qbk5aga",
      "content": "• Queen of Jhansi and leader in the Revolt of 1857."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xxjyc0g",
      "content": "• Fought bravely against British forces."
    },
    {
      "id": "lz7npe9",
